      "content": "That's a helpful starting point. To get more specific, I'm looking to see if the literature differentiates how these selection pressures manifested in specific, major ancestral groups. For instance, when looking at traits like impulse control or group-oriented social behavior, are there certain population clusters—perhaps sub-Saharan African or East Asian lineages—where the data suggests more pronounced biological trends or \"archetypical\" patterns compared to Western European populations? I'm trying to see if the research identifies any specific genetic markers that correlate with those divergent behavioral profiles.",
